#!/bin/bash
# mkinitcpio install hook for sleep-drain's safe boot (sleepdrain-safe.hook).
# Only sleep-drain-safe adds it, to its own image (mkinitcpio -A); the regular
# initramfs doesn't have it.

build() {
    add_module overlay
    add_module btrfs
    add_binary blockdev
    add_runscript
}

help() {
    cat <<HELPEOF
With "sleepdrain.safe" on the kernel command line: the root's block device is
made read-only, and / and the fstab's btrfs subvolumes get RAM overlays.
HELPEOF
}
